<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Sockets on cesun.life</title><link>https://example.org/tags/sockets/</link><description>Recent content in Sockets on cesun.life</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 18 May 2022 17:00:37 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://example.org/tags/sockets/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Linux Socket System</title><link>https://example.org/socket/</link><pubDate>Wed, 18 May 2022 17:00:37 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/socket/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A socket is a file descriptor representing one endpoint of a communications channel.
Programs create one with &lt;code&gt;socket(2)&lt;/code&gt;, then usually bind or connect it and use
&lt;code&gt;read(2)&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;write(2)&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;send(2)&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;recv(2)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-c" data-lang="c"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; sockfd &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;socket&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; domain, &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; type, &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; protocol);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The domain selects an address family such as &lt;code&gt;AF_INET&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AF_INET6&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AF_UNIX&lt;/code&gt;, or
&lt;code&gt;AF_NETLINK&lt;/code&gt;. The type selects a semantic such as &lt;code&gt;SOCK_STREAM&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;SOCK_DGRAM&lt;/code&gt;, or
&lt;code&gt;SOCK_SEQPACKET&lt;/code&gt;; the protocol normally selects a concrete protocol within that
combination, or &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; selects the default.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>